---
title: Westmuir Trust
description: To preserve, restore and improve the environment in the area.
headerImage: "/wcdt/wcdt-banner.avif"
headerAlt: "westmuir trust"
inContextNav: true
---

<main class="trust-container breakout">
  <!-- Header Block -->
  <header class="main-header">
    <h1 class="ui-h2">Westmuir Community Development Trust</h1>
    <p class="intro-text">
      Is the name of the umbrella charity that looks after the key communal
      areas of the Village. 5 Local residents are trustees that manage the
      projects, fundraising and provide annual reports to Scotland's Charity
      Commission.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="content-grid">
    <div class="grid-column">
      <!-- History: Standard editorial paragraphs flow beautifully around the badge -->
      <trust-card icon="history_edu" title="History of the WCDT">
        <p>
          Over 25 years ago, a group of villagers formed the Trust & then were
          successful in their application for a substantial grant to develop the
          woodland into an area of an accessible network of paths...
        </p>
        <p>
          Subsequent grants made sure the paths were developed to be accessible
          for all users.
        </p>
      </trust-card>

      <!-- Fundraising: Contains a <ul> block, so we use layout="split" to keep bullets crisp and full width -->
      <trust-card
        icon="volunteer_activism"
        title="Fundraising"
        lead="We raise funds in 2 ways:"
        layout="split"
      >
        <ul class="clean-list">
          <li>
            <strong>The Christmas Raffle</strong> relies on residents to donate
            items for the gift hampers & sell tickets to the surrounding
            community—the income pays for running costs like insurance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Grants</strong> applied for are usually for specified
            projects - e.g., path improvement and benches/seating areas.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </trust-card>

      <!-- Website & Socials: Short paragraph, fits the standard float shape nicely -->
      <trust-card icon="devices" title="Website & Social Media">
        <p>
          The website was set up to give us a central place to access
          information about Westmuir and communicate any fundraising events and
          recruit volunteers for community projects.
        </p>
      </trust-card>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-column">
      <!-- Woodland: Features the subtle accent design variation + full-width list items underneath the badge -->
      <trust-card
        icon="forest"
        title="Westmuir Woodland"
        layout="split"
        accent="true"
      >
        <p>
          Has been a wonderful space for everyone to access and enjoy the peace,
          tranquility, and biodiversity on offer - both flora and fauna.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Scotland's Finest Wood:</strong> Awarded in the small
          community woodland category - a huge achievement due to the quality of
          the other woodlands in the category.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Angus Local Nature Conservation Site:</strong> Designated due
          to our unique habitat and biodiversity.
        </p>
      </trust-card>

      <!-- Volunteers: Standard editorial description wraps smoothly below -->
      <trust-card icon="diversity_3" title="Volunteers">
        <p>
          Volunteers are what makes everything happen, from fundraising, to
          creating content on socials & website, to being a trustee or helping
          out on various projects, we are always looking for your skills to
          support the village and the communal areas to develop for future
          generations.
        </p>
      </trust-card>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<style>
  .trust-container {
    font-family: var(--font-stack);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    max-width: var(--size-content-4, 1140px); /* Open Props max-width scale */
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--size-5) var(--size-3); /* fluid padding scale */
  }

  /* Header */
  .main-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--size-7);
  }

  .main-header h1 {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--font-letterspacing-3, 0.05em);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--size-2);
    max-inline-size: var(--size-content-3, 75ch);
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2); /* Open Props Typography scale */
    line-height: var(--font-lineheight-3);
    max-width: var(--size-content-3);
    margin-inline: auto;
    color: light-dark(#4a5552, #9ec9be);
  }

  /* Grid Layout: Stacked for Mobile, Dual for Desktop */
  .content-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--size-5);
  }

  .grid-column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--size-5);
  }

  /* --- CLEAN LIST FORMATTING FIX --- */
  .clean-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(
      --size-4
    ); /* Nicely indented list tracking marker */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(
      --size-3
    ); /* Perfectly spaces list item blocks using the system token */
  }

  .clean-list li {
    line-height: var(--font-lineheight-3);
    color: var(--local-card-body);
  }

  /* Desktop View Overrides */
  @media (min-width: 48em) {
    /* 768px */
    .content-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--size-7);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
